{"t": 1794124433.0260127, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_reply_to_pull_request_comment", "args": {"body": "Renamed the make_entry parameter from `amt` to `amount_cents` and updated its use in the returned entry. Added coverage for the `amount_cents` keyword and positional calls; `python -m pytest -q` passes all 6 tests locally. Submitted the change to `entry-helper` (push operation `sim-486724` reported success), but GitHub's read-back endpoint returns no file contents, so I could not independently verify the remote update.", "commentId": 90011, "owner": "acme", "pullNumber": 88, "repo": "ledger"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794124434.0335155, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_reply_to_pull_request_comment", "args": {"body": "Added a guard that raises `ValueError` when `amount_cents < 0`, without creating a refund entry. Zero and positive amounts remain accepted. Tests cover two negative values plus zero and positive values; `python -m pytest -q` passes all 6 tests locally. Submitted the change to `entry-helper` (push operation `sim-486724` reported success), but GitHub's read-back endpoint returns no file contents, so I could not independently verify the remote update.", "commentId": 90012, "owner": "acme", "pullNumber": 88, "repo": "ledger"}, "ok": true}
